                <pb facs="0233" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5315/248.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Fletcher to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-06-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 16,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Fletcher states he is informed that representatives of the groups here have
                    telegraphed their principals recommending American participation in the present
                    loan, and adds that if such is the agreement, some one here should be authorized
                    to sign for the American group without waiting for arrival American
                    representative, as such delay would jeopardize successful issue.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
